topic.p:
The default empty array disables this behavior.
Clearing an assigned array stops further overrides and keeps the current stored PreferredMinSize;
it does not restore the value from before assignment.
Normal bounds measurement still applies, so children, elements and margins can require more space than the selected preference.
With zero margins, a nonzero level is retained at its effective minimum and lowered below that minimum;
growing to the next level's effective minimum admits that level.
